# Git worktrees live inside the repo, so Prettier walks a second checkout of the
# whole tree and reports its files as unformatted. Both paths are gitignored, so
# CI never sees them — but `bun run format:check` fails locally for anyone with a
# worktree open, which reads as a red lint step on an otherwise clean tree.
.claude/worktrees/
.worktrees/

# Same shape, different file: Claude Code rewrites this one itself as permissions
# are granted, so its formatting is not ours to own. It is gitignored, so CI on a
# fresh clone never sees it — but locally it was the single warning standing
# between a clean tree and a green `bun run format:check`.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Impeccable design-hook cache, rewritten on every edit it inspects.
.impeccable/

# Vendored Oxlint plugin — a verbatim copy of the anti-slop rules, kept
# byte-identical to upstream so a re-install is a clean diff rather than a
# reformat. Its own style (tabs, semicolons, double quotes) is the opposite of
# this repo's, and reformatting it would make every future update conflict.
# Same reasoning as `server.ts` above: keep two formatters off the same files.
tools/oxlint/anti-slop/
